The attached image displays flow cytometry histograms illustrating the expression of co-stimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). The gray lines represent BMDCs incubated with medium control, while the black lines show BMDCs treated with Nano-11. Nano-11 treatment resulted in a slight increase in CD40 expression and a significant upregulation of CD80 and CD86. This indicates that Nano-11 activates dendritic cells, which is a critical step in initiating an effective immune response by enabling antigen presentation and subsequent T cell activation.